Docker build command has cache, it only updates the new parts

Every part of the docker file is a layer, and if a layer is not changed, 
it will use the cached version of that layer.

when docker builds a docker file, it checks each line and if the line is 
not changed, it will use the cached version of that layer.
If the line is changed, it will rebuild that layer and all the layers 
after that line.

Volumes are folders on the host machine that persist and can be shared between different containers. You can map folders inside of containers to volumnes.

Volumes persist even if the container is stopped or deleted. To accomplish this you have to setup named volumnes

